{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Gurugram-based Omli, focused on developing artificial intelligence (AI) infrastructure for children's speech and language development, has raised $1.5 million in a seed funding round led by India Quotient, with participation from General Catalyst. The funding announcement was made on 17th June 2026.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Founded in 2025 by Shivam Munshi and Siddhant Garg, Omli aims to fill a notable gap in the AI landscape by creating speech models tailored specifically for young children. Most existing commercial speech recognition systems are predominantly trained on adult voices, leading to inaccuracies when interacting with children, whose speech patterns and tones differ significantly from those of adults.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Omli's flagship application, OmliKids, enables children aged three to ten years to engage in voice-based conversations with an AI companion named Doro. Distinct from other children's digital products that heavily rely on games or video content, Omli is positioning its app as a conversational platform designed to enhance speaking skills and logical thinking. The app has already achieved over 500,000 downloads on the Google Play Store within a few months of its launch.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 To address the challenges associated with conventional speech models, Omli has developed VedAnsh-v1, a proprietary speech-to-text and voice activity detection system specifically designed for children's voices. This innovative model has shown significant improvements in word error rates compared to existing commercial systems when tested with children's speech. Co-founder Siddhant Garg emphasized the company's ambition to achieve adult-grade accuracy in children's speech recognition, including support for Indian accents and vernacular languages.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 With a current team of around 15 employees, Omli is in the process of developing the next generation of its speech model and aims to expand into conversational intelligence systems that can adapt in real-time to a child's speaking pace and communication patterns. The startup also plans to create speech-based screening tools to help parents and educators identify articulation challenges early on. Shivam Munshi noted that today's children are often seen silently scrolling on screens, underscoring the need for }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 technology}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
