{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 MENLO PARK \u8211  Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P., an entity associated with Lightspeed Venture Partners, reported the sale of Netskope Inc. (NASDAQ:NTSK) Class A common stock totaling approximately $15.1 million, according to a recent SEC filing. The date of these transactions was 12th June 2026 and 15th June 2026, as Netskope shares traded at $8.95, down roughly 60% over the past year and near its 52-week low of $7.67.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 On 12th June 2026, Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P. converted 1,650,000 shares of Class B common stock into Class A common stock for no additional consideration. Following this conversion, the fund sold 1,313,827 shares of Netskope Class A common stock at a weighted average price of $9.19 per share. Two days later, on 15th June 2026, Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P. sold an additional 336,173 shares of Class A common stock at a weighted average price of $9.00 per share. The total value of these sales amounted to $15,099,627, with the weighted average prices for the transactions ranging between $9.00 and $9.19. Following these sales, Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P. holds no Class A common stock.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 While Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P. has divested its Class A common stock, several other Lightspeed entities continue to hold significant amounts of Netskope Class B common stock. These Class B shares are convertible into Class A common stock on a one-for-one basis at the option of the holder or automatically on 19th September 2035. As of 12th June 2026, these and other related Lightspeed entities collectively held 62,843,207 shares of Class B common stock, representing potential Class A shares.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In other recent developments, Netskope reported annual recurring revenue (ARR) of $845 million, reflecting a 29% year-over-year increase, which met general market expectations but fell short of some analysts\u8217  estimates. The company\u8217 s total revenue reached approximately $202 million, marking a 28% year-over-year growth and slightly surpassing market forecasts. Despite these figures, several financial firms have adjusted their price targets for Netskope, with TD Cowen reducing its target from $25 to $19 while maintaining a Buy rating, citing the ARR miss and the exit of the CFO as influencing factors.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 BMO Capital and RBC Capital both lowered their targets to $13, maintaining an Outperform rating, with concerns about the company\u8217 s ARR growth and market competition. Piper Sandler decreased its target to $18, noting strong new logo ARR growth and traction with new AI products but highlighting challenges with sales force productivity. Mizuho also cut its target to $13, acknowledging the modest revenue beat but pointing out it was the smallest upside since Netskope became a public company. These developments illustrate the varied analyst perspectives on Netskope\u8217 s recent performance.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
